From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: KYTY_GPU_SUBMIT_THREAD hands command buffers to Vulkan
 from a thread of their own

The GPU thread runs on one PS4 core at 100% in heavy games (DREDGE: about 850
submits a second, and ioctl is 10% of the thread). With KYTY_GPU_SUBMIT_THREAD
set, Submit queues the command buffer and its tick, and a submit thread calls
vkQueueSubmit in the same order; the GPU thread goes on recording at once.

- Host waits for a tick first wait until its work reached the queue
  (MasterSemaphore before-wait hook).
- Every other queue user (the present scheduler, waitIdle, OpenXR, RenderDoc)
  first drains the queued submits, so the queue keeps the order of the work:
  presenting reads frames the GPU thread copied.
---
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/graphicContext.h
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/graphicContext.h
@@ -57,6 +57,16 @@
 	Common::Mutex                      queue_mutex;
 	uint32_t                           queue_family = static_cast<uint32_t>(-1);
 	vk::Queue                          queue        = nullptr;
+	// KYTY_GPU_SUBMIT_THREAD: the GPU thread's command buffers reach the queue from a thread of
+	// their own. Whoever else uses the queue first waits until those queued before have reached
+	// it (DrainQueuedSubmits), so the queue keeps the order of the work. Set once at start.
+	void (*drain_queued_submits)(void* context) = nullptr;
+	void*  drain_queued_submits_context        = nullptr;
+	void   DrainQueuedSubmits() const {
+		if (drain_queued_submits != nullptr) {
+			drain_queued_submits(drain_queued_submits_context);
+		}
+	}
 
 	[[nodiscard]] const vk::PhysicalDeviceProperties& GetPhysicalDeviceProperties() const {
 		return physical_device_properties;
